    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0417" n="327" xml:id="pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 294/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Observer on the Rhineland High Commission</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Noyes</hi>)<anchor n="37"
                        xml:id="d279-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-17T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Owing to the fact that the treaty has not been ratified and that the United
                    States is not likely to have a delegate on the Rhineland Commission, and in
                    accord with the idea of reducing so far as possible American personnel in
                    Europe, the Department has decided to relieve you as American observer on the
                    Commission as you recently requested. After consultation with the Secretary of
                    War it has been decided that General Allen should take your place as observer
                    with the Commission. It is believed that he already has capable assistants but
                    should he desire to retain the services of any of your staff, this may be
                    arranged at least temporarily. You should therefore plan to leave as soon as
                    your work can be conveniently turned over to General Allen.<anchor n="38"
                        xml:id="d279-f2"/></p>
                <p>Your April 29th, 5 P.M.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d279-f3"/> Expenses up to time of
                    leaving should probably be entered as a lump sum or in accord with the practice
                    of the regularly delegated Commissioners.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d279-f1" n="37" type="source" xml:id="d279-f1-content">
                <p>Via the Embassy in France as no. 948.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d279-f2" n="38" xml:id="d279-f2-content">
                <p>General Allen cabled on June 16 that he had relieved Noyes June 3 (file no.
                    862t.01/119).</p>
            </note>
